.SH NAME
kronein-util \- manual page for kronein-util v31.1.0
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kronein-util
[\fI\,options\/\fR] [\fI\,command\/\fR]
.br
.B kronein-util
[\fI\,options\/\fR] \fI\,grind <hex-block-header>\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Kronein Core kronein\-util utility version v31.1.0
.PP
The kronein\-util tool provides Kronein\-related functionality that does not rely on the ability to access a running node. Available [commands] are listed below.
.SH OPTIONS
.HP
\fB\-help\fR
.IP
Print this help message and exit (also \fB\-h\fR or \-?)
.HP
\fB\-version\fR
.IP
Print version and exit
.PP
Chain selection options:
.HP
\fB\-chain=\fR<chain>
.IP
Use the chain <chain> (default: main). Allowed values: main, testnet4,
signet, regtest
.HP
\fB\-signet\fR
.IP
Use the signet chain. Equivalent to \fB\-chain\fR=\fI\,signet\/\fR. Note that the network
is defined by the \fB\-signetchallenge\fR parameter
.HP
\fB\-signetchallenge\fR
.IP
Blocks must provide a Taproot witness satisfying this P2TR scriptPubKey
(only for signet networks; defaults to the project Signet
challenge)
.HP
\fB\-signetseednode\fR
.IP
Specify a seed node for the signet network, in the hostname[:port]
format, e.g. sig.net:1234 (may be used multiple times)
.HP
\fB\-testnet4\fR
.IP
Use the testnet4 chain. Equivalent to \fB\-chain\fR=\fI\,testnet4\/\fR.
.PP
Commands:
.IP
grind
.IP
Perform proof of work on hex header string
